    "caption": "Here’s a tasty and satisfying pasta dish that you can make at home with the simplest ingredients.\n\nAnchor Salted Butter, parmesan cheese, lemon, chopped parsley, and your choice of pasta (we used rigatoni for this one) come together in this delightful Brown Butter Lemon Pasta. Brown butter makes everything better because, with its longer and slower cooking process, a nuttier and slightly sweeter flavor takes over. It’s truly one of life’s simplest pleasures. Head over to #TheMarketplace today and try out this recipe soon! We hope you love it as much as we do.\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 8 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 kg rigatoni pasta\n1 pack (226g) Anchor Salted Butter, cubed and divided\n1 fresh lemon, thinly sliced\n½ cup parmesan cheese, finely grated\nFinely chopped parsley and fresh cracked black pepper to garnish\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Cook rigatoni until al dente, 2 mins. less than package instructions. Reserve 2 cups pasta water. Drain the rest and set aside.\n2. Melt half of the Anchor Salted Butter in a saucepan over low heat. Add lemon slices and stir until the butter begins to brown. Set lemon slices aside.\n3. In the pan of lemon brown butter, mix reserved pasta water and remaining butter until emulsified. \n4. Stir rigatoni and parmesan in the sauce until creamy. Transfer to a plate. Top with more parmesan, cooked lemon slices, parsley, and fresh cracked black pepper.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
