    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "TMP Anniversary",
    "caption": "Having guests over? Impress them by making this Crimson Grape Galette with a bunch of DJ Forry California Red Seedless Grapes.\n\nThe tip to not getting the galette’s bottom soggy is to brush the interior crust with egg white to seal the dough and prevent excess and unwanted moisture to soak into the crust. Grapes that are cooked down until soft yield a unique sweetness that’s deep, rich, and sophisticated. Give your guests a dessert to remember and grab all the ingredients that you need for this galette at their freshest from #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 2 hours\nYield: 8 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the dough:\n2 cups all-purpose flour\n1 tsp. salt\n½ tsp. cinnamon powder\n1 cup cold unsalted butter, cubed\n4-6 tbsps. ice water\n1 beaten egg for egg wash\nBrown sugar for sprinkling\n\nFor the filling:\n4 cups DJ Forry California Red Seedless Grapes, halved\n3-4 tbsps. granulated sugar\n2 tbsps. cornstarch\n1 tbsp. fresh lemon juice\n1 tsp. vanilla extract, optional\nWhipped cream and fresh mint to garnish\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a food processor, mix flour, salt, and cinnamon. Pulse with cold butter until sandy. Add cold water and knead into a smooth dough. Wrap and chill for 1 hour.\n2. In a pan over medium heat, simmer DJ Forry California Red Seedless Grapes, sugar, lemon juice, and vanilla. Thicken juices with cornstarch, then set aside to cool. Preheat oven to 180°C.\n3. On a parchment-lined tray, roll dough to a large rectangle about ¼-inch thick. Spread grape filling, leaving a 1-inch border all around. Fold edges, brush egg wash, and sprinkle brown sugar. \n4. Bake for 30-40 mins. until golden brown and bubbly. Cool and garnish with whipped cream and fresh mint.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
