    "layoutCode": "ANV6",
    "layoutName": "Yang Chow Cauliflower Fried Rice",
    "category": "RECIPE",
    "categorySource": "inferred",
    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "TMP Anniversary",
    "caption": "Now that the holidays are a stone’s throw away, some of us might want to opt for healthier dishes before then. And if you’re craving some Chinese fried rice, a simple way to add more fiber to your meal is to replace the rice with Emborg Cauliflower Rice, which comes ready-to-cook from the packet. Because it comes in a convenient rice form, there is no need to chop any cauliflowers, making clean-up a breeze.\n\nSeasoned with all the right ingredients and complete with slices of savory chorizo, it’ll be tough to tell the difference between this Yang Chow Cauliflower Fried Rice and its original form. Find Emborg products, along with this pre-chopped cauliflower rice, at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 4 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the fried rice:\n2 tbsps. vegetable oil\n1 red onion, diced\n3 cloves garlic, minced\n½ cup chorizo macao, thinly sliced \n½ cup small shrimp, peeled and deveined\n2 eggs, beaten\n½ cup green peas\n½ cup carrots, diced\n1 pack (450g) Emborg Cauliflower Rice\nThinly sliced scallions to garnish\n\nFor the seasoning sauce:\n2 tbsps. soy sauce\n2 tbsps. oyster sauce\n2 tbsps. Chinese cooking wine\n2 tsps. sesame oil\n\nProcedure\n1. Mix sauce ingredients in a bowl. Set aside.\n2. Heat oil in a large wok over medium-high heat. Sauté onions and garlic until fragrant, then add chorizo macao and shrimp. Cook for 3-5 mins. then push to one side.\n3. Add eggs and lightly scramble. Combine all ingredients and add green peas and carrots. Cook until softened.\n4. Add Emborg Cauliflower Rice and pour sauce all over. Stir-fry until the fried rice is tender and well-seasoned. Transfer to a bowl and garnish with scallions.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
