    "layoutCode": "ANV7",
    "layoutName": "Corned Beef Mac & Cheese",
    "category": "RECIPE",
    "categorySource": "inferred",
    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "TMP Anniversary",
    "caption": "Spruce up your mac and cheese and give it a meaty twist with some PL Aguila Corned Beef!\n\nThis Corned Beef Mac & Cheese gives the classic pasta dish more depth, flavor, and body. The play of textures turns it into a meal that needs no accompaniment. With mac and cheese being typically perceived as a side, the addition of corned beef completes it and makes the dish a meal on its own. Find PL Aguila Corned Beef, along with all the other items that you need for this beefy and cheesy pasta dish, at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour\nYield: 6 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n450g elbow macaroni\n1 tbsp. oil\n1 can (350g) PL Aguila Corned Beef\n1 cup shredded cheddar, plus more\n1 cup shredded mozzarella, plus more\n2 cups whole milk\n2 tbsps. butter, plus more for brushing\n1 tbsp. all-purpose flour\n¼ cup panko, seasoned\nSalt and white pepper to taste\nFresh basil to garnish\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Preheat oven to 190°C.\n2. Cook macaroni according to package instructions. Drain and set aside.\n3. Heat oil in a cast-iron pan over medium heat. Cook PL Aguila Corned Beef until lightly toasted. Remove from pan and set aside.\n4. In the same pan, stir butter, milk, cheddar, mozzarella, flour, salt and pepper until thick and melted. Add macaroni and corned beef, then mix.\n5. Top with panko and extra cheese. Bake for 20-25 mins. until golden. Garnish with fresh basil.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
